                        "Although early econometric models posited that tariffs safeguard domestic employment (Brown, 2018), subsequent empirical analyses demonstrate that retaliatory duties precipitate both inflation and net trade contractions (Davies, 2020; Chen, 2022).",
                        "First, Brown had an idea about trade. Second, Davies had a different idea. Third, Chen wrote another paper on the subject.",
                        "Brown says tariffs are bad. Davies also says tariffs are bad. Chen agrees with them both in his book."
